  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jordan: Feasibility Study: Virtual Power Plant, through Enon Management, LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study (FS) for Kawar Energy (Kawar), a leading renewable energy company in Jordan, to develop a pilot project for a virtual power plant, a cloud-based system to control, integrate, and aggregate the output of selected solar photovoltaic and battery energy storage systems that the Grantee owns and operates throughout Jordan. This FS will help Kawar anticipate and manage energy transmission during peak and off-peak times more efficiently, and will provide a model for broadly applicable improvements to Jordans electrical grid, which will help reduce the countrys substantial reliance on foreign-sourced energy and fuel.</narrative>
  </description>
